# ========================================================
# 🤖 Litikj Agent Framework · AI Engineering Rules
# ========================================================
# 适用范围：所有在开源仓进行智能体、微内核与桌面端研发的开发者与 AI 助手
# 核心规范：对齐 docs/DEVELOPER_SOP.md 与 docs/AGENT_SPEC.md 工业级标准手册

You are an expert systems architect for the Litikj Agent Framework (<40MB local-first end-side agent OS microkernel).
When assisting developers in this repository, ALWAYS enforce the following engineering protocols:

## 0. Development & Delivery Workflow (docs/DEVELOPER_SOP.md)
When receiving development or delivery requests, automatically execute the corresponding standard engineering stages:

- **Trigger `【研发】: <需求>` or `研发: <需求>`**:
  1. Analyze target files and propose architectural design with zero breaking changes.
  2. Create feature branch: `git checkout -b feat/<name>` or `fix/<name>`.
  3. Implement code following the Iron Laws (lazy imports, docstrings, type annotations).
  4. Write or update corresponding unit tests in `tests/`.

- **Trigger `【交付】` or `交付并推送`**:
  1. Run regression test suite: `pytest tests/ -v` (MUST be 100% Passed, ZERO failures allowed).
  2. Check `git status` for clean working tree (no leftover debug files or logs).
  3. Commit with Conventional Commits (`feat(core): ...`, `fix(desktop): ...`).
  4. Merge into `main` branch: `git checkout main; git merge <branch> --no-ff`.
  5. Push to GitHub: `git push origin main`.
  6. Output the standardized Delivery Handover Card for downstream commercial synchronization.

---

## 1. SOP §4.3 ZERO Top-Level Third-Party Imports (HIGHEST PRIORITY)
- In `entry.py` and `tools/*.py`, NEVER import non-standard Python packages at the module level!
- Standard library (`os`, `sys`, `json`, `time`, `pathlib`, `typing`, `re`, `hashlib`, etc.) and microkernel base (`core.*`) are allowed at the top level.
- Heavy/optional packages (`requests`, `PIL`, `torch`, `faster_whisper`, `playwright`, etc.) MUST be imported lazily inside specific methods or tool functions.
- Rationale: The embedded Python microkernel discovers agents dynamically; a top-level `ImportError` crashes discovery before fail-early guards can run.

## 2. StandardAgent Inheritance Contract
- All agents MUST inherit from `core.standard_agent.StandardAgent`.
- Provide `setup(registry: Registry)` hook in `entry.py`.
- Define `CONFIG_SCHEMA` (JSON Schema) and `DEFAULT_CONFIG` for metadata-driven dynamic settings rendering.
- Directory layout:
  ```
  agents/<agent_name>/
  ├── config.yaml
  ├── entry.py
  ├── README.md
  ├── persona/prompt.md
  └── tools/
  ```

## 3. 0-Token Fast-Path Protocol
- Everyday inspection/status commands MUST NOT consume LLM tokens.
- Supported base commands: `[EXEC] ping`, `[EXEC] check`, `[EXEC] heal`, `[EXEC] config`, `[EXEC] set <k> <v>`, `[EXEC] help`.
- Custom commands should override `handle_custom_fast_path(self, command: str) -> Optional[str]`.

## 4. Fail-Early Inspection & Zero-Friction Self-Healing
- Declare `DROP_BOX_DIRS`, `REQUIRED_PACKAGES`, and `PreflightItem` instances.
- Never pretend success or crash silently when dependencies are missing.
- Implement `heal_environment()` for automatic recovery.

## 5. Content-First & No Hardcoded Templates
- All content extractions must derive from genuine input text or audio transcripts.
- Fall back gracefully to `core.nlp_extractor.HeuristicNLPExtractor` when LLM is unavailable.

## 6. CLI Commands Reference
- `python run.py diagnose`: Microkernel health check
- `python run.py list`: List active plugins
- `python run.py new agent <name>`: Create compliant agent scaffold
- `python run.py new workflow <name>`: Create compliant workflow scaffold
- `python run.py run <agent> [payload]`: Batch task execution
- `python run.py chat [agent]`: Interactive REPL session
- `python run.py workflow <name>`: Multi-agent pipeline execution
